
You are a senior audio/video synchronization engineer.

My current dubbing pipeline produces:

- Input video: ~1:35
- Dubbed audio: ~1:54
- Final video: ~1:35 (audio truncated)

So audio drift is accumulating and ffmpeg is trimming it.

Your task: Diagnose and permanently fix timing drift and truncation.

Implement professional-grade alignment similar to YouTube Auto-Dub.

